  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Study visits on Animal Welfare to the Netherlands</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of the project is to implement two study visits in the Netherlands with a focus on animal welfare regulations and the control of their implementation in the poultry- and dairy sectors. These visits aim to provide:i.	Insights into the institutional structure for implementing legal rules on the welfare of farmed animals.ii.	Experience with the challenges and best practices in applying animal welfare rules in livestock production.iii.	Knowledge of the organisation and execution of official controls to verify compliance with animal welfare standards.iv.	Insight in training systems for staff involved in the care, transportation, and humane killing of farmed animals.v.	Fostered bilateral cooperation through links between members of the delegation and Dutch experts involved with the study visit. This project complements the Swiss-Ukrainian Quality FOOD Trade program (QFTP), funded by the Swiss State Secretariat for Economic Affairs (SECO), with contributions from the private sector in Ukraine. This project is a joint effort to improve the knowledge capacity of Ukrainian government authorities. As result of the two visits the Ukrainian delegation will learn how the Netherlands (EU country) implements animal welfare rules and performance of control measures for verification of compliance with these rules. This project contributes to:&#x2022;	SDG 8: Promoting inclusive and sustainable economic growth by supporting productive activities and decent job creation in the animal welfare sector.&#x2022;	SDG 12: Ensuring sustainable consumption and production patterns by implementing humane and ethical animal welfare practices.&#x2022;	SDG 15: Protecting life on land by ensuring the ethical treatment and welfare of farmed animals, contributing to biodiversity and ecological balance.</narrative>
  </description>
